{"etape": 15, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T11:22:46.172463Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Here's the breakdown for the change (3 passengers):\n\n**New business class prices (per passenger):**\n| Flight | Date | Business |\n|---|---|---|\n| HAT190 IAH→LAS | May 24 | $464 |\n| HAT047 LAS→SEA | May 24 | $202 |\n| HAT021 SEA→JFK | May 26 | $290 |\n| HAT279 JFK→IAH | May 27 | $241 |\n| **Subtotal** | | **$1,197** |\n\n**New total:** $1,197 × 3 = **$3,591**\n**Original flight cost:** $527 × 3 = **$1,581**\n\n**Estimated additional cost: $2,010**\n\nA couple of notes:\n- Your existing insurance and 1 checked bag carry over. As a gold member in business class, you'd get 4 free checked bags per passenger, so no baggage fees apply.\n- To proceed, I'll need a payment method for the difference. Which would you like to use: **Visa ending 3422**, **Mastercard ending 9448**, or **gift card** (only $62 balance)?\n\nPlease confirm and let me know the payment method, and I'll make the change."}, "resultat": "Wow, that's a significant increase. An additional cost of $2,010 is much higher than I was expecting. I was hoping to keep the extra cost under $1000.\n\nIs there any way to get the total extra cost down? Perhaps a different flight option for the IAH to SEA leg that's still on May 24th and in business class, but more affordable? I'm really trying to stick to my budget here.", "erreur": null}
